60" y2="166"/><circle cx="340.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="340.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1840: After 34 Comanche leaders are massacred at peace talks in San Antonio, Buffalo Hump leads the Great Raid of 1840 to the Gulf coast; the Comanches are caught at the Battle of Plum Creek.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="500.0" x2="500.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="500.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="500.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1842: On 11 September Adrián Woll's 1,400 Mexican troops capture San Antonio; Texans fight at the Battle of Salado Creek while 53 surrendered volunteers are massacred nearby.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>1845: On 29 December Texas is annexed and admitted as the 28th state of the United States; power passes from the republic on 19 February 1846.</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1836 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1845 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1835</span><span class="rf-text">On 2 October hostilities between Texian settlers and Mexican troops open at the Battle of Gonzales, the first engagement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas-revolution">Texas Revolution</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1836</span><span class="rf-text">On 2 March the Convention of 1836 proclaims the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> Declaration of Independence; David G. Burnet becomes interim president.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1836</span><span class="rf-text">On 21 April major fighting ends, and the Treaties of Velasco, signed by Santa Anna as a prisoner, secure <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>'s independence, which the Mexican Congress refuses to recognise.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1837</span><span class="rf-text">On 3 March President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a> appoints Alcée La Branche chargé d'affaires, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> officially recognising the republic.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1839</span><span class="rf-text">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirabeau-b-lamar">Mirabeau B. Lamar</a> moves the capital to the new town of Austin; the Lone Star Flag is adopted and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recognises <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> on 25 September.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1840</span><span class="rf-text">After 34 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> leaders are massacred at peace talks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a>, Buffalo Hump leads the Great Raid of 1840 to the Gulf coast; the Comanches are caught at the Battle of Plum Creek.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1842</span><span class="rf-text">On 11 September Adrián Woll's 1,400 Mexican troops capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a>; Texans fight at the Battle of Salado Creek while 53 surrendered volunteers are massacred nearby.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1845</span><span class="rf-text">On 29 December <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> is annexed and admitted as the 28th state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>; power passes from the republic on 19 February 1846.</span></li></ol>
